WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.760
- [Soldier] Yeah.
(rocket blasting)

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.060
- [Narrator] This is the US-made
Patriot Air Defense System.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.280
Since two were delivered
to Ukraine in April,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.540
it's proving to be an indispensable
tool in Kyiv's arsenal.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.560
That's because the system

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.420
is defending Ukraine's ground troops,

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.370
cities, and critical infrastructure,

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.920
amid a barrage of Russian attacks.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.260
So why does the Patriot have an advantage

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.900
over other air defense systems?

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.900
Let's break it down.

00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:28.080
"At the start of the war,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.710
Ukraine relied on a stockpile
of Soviet-era defense systems.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.800
Those weapons can target
slower-moving aerial targets

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.050
such as drones and cruise missiles,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.190
but they've struggled to combat

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.620
faster-moving ballistic missiles.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.050
Now, Patriot systems are
helping Ukrainian forces

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.000
to intercept those projectiles,"

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.580
and that's according to a
Ukrainian Air Defense Commander

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.385
interviewed by "The Wall Street Journal."

00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:54.302
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:56.935 --> 00:00:58.560
- Narrator] Here's how it works.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.410
Patriot missiles consist
of multiple components.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.593
Three of its main parts sit
on top of truck platforms.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.160
The radar tracks missiles
and other targets.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.280
It can detect aircraft up to 62 miles away

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.070
and ballistic missiles
more than 100 miles away.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.160
It sends data to the
engagement control station,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.350
that unit then processes the information

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.510
before sending it to
the launching station,

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.773
which can carry up to 16 missiles.

00:01:24.773 --> 00:01:28.690
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.487
- Narrator] Military analysts say,

00:01:42.487 --> 00:01:44.310
"The system has outperformed

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.804
initial expectations in Ukraine."

00:01:46.804 --> 00:01:50.721
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:54.737
- [Narrator] Also known as the Kinzhal,

00:01:54.737 --> 00:01:59.490
the Kh-47 is one of Russia's
most advanced weapons.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.440
On May 16th, a Patriot detected

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.840
six Russian Kinzhal ballistic missiles

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.810
at a distance of around 125 miles.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.760
The system launched interceptors

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.500
destroying all of them.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.570
Patriots in Ukraine fire at targets

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.360
using two different types of interceptors,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.430
PAC-2 and PAC-3.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.820
PAC-2 downs targets through
blast fragmentation,

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.600
and PAC-3 uses hit-to-kill
technology instead.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.450
By combining the Patriot with
other air defense systems,

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.050
Ukraine is now fending off most
aerial threats against Kyiv.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.310
However, the Patriot does
have some disadvantages.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.580
It's by far the most
expensive single weapon system

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.010
that the US has supplied to Ukraine.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.920
Each Patriot system
costs around $1 billion

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.950
and takes two years to build.
(missile blasting)

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.460
The missiles fired out of the
Patriot are expensive too.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.720
Each PAC-3 costs around $4.1 million.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.250
The high cost per missile

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.130
and the relatively small
number of missiles in a battery

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:03.300
means that Patriot operators
cannot shoot at every target.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.330
In addition, the Patriot
requires a lot of manpower.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.660
The systems need as many
as 90 soldiers to operate,

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.570
but the control station can
be operated in the field

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.743
by as few as three.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.070
Gaining more batteries could help Kyiv

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.770
in a number of ways amid
a counter-offensive,

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.960
namely, being able to
protect ground troops

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.770
from aerial threats as they
push to retake territory.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.350
This summer, the US announced
a new military package

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.943
worth up to $500 million.

00:03:31.147 --> 00:03:33.900
"The aid will include
ammunition for Patriot systems,"

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.450
according to a statement
from the Pentagon.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.700
There are at least two
full Patriot systems

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.830
operating in Ukraine.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.140
In July, Germany
announced it would provide

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.483
two additional Patriot Missile Launches.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.600
Ukrainian President Vladimir Zelensky

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.297
has said, "The country
wants as many as 50."

